  Before you ship it, there's a conflict with the README. It says field names in [38;5;153mGET /users[39m are part of the contract,
  and that changes go through a versioned endpoint. It lists three consumers: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later),
  and the nightly partner export. Changing the field in place would break any of them that read [38;5;153muserId[39m. You can't
  force-update older iOS builds or the partner's job.

